    $q$A piece of work can be completed by x men in y days. If there were 6 men more, the work could be finished in 4 days less. If there were 10 men less, the work would take 10 days more. What is the value of (x + y)?
(a) 68
(b) 72
(c) 74
(d) 80$q$,
    $q$["68","72","74","80"]$q$::jsonb,
    2,
    $q$C$q$,
    $q$1. Let total work W = x × y.
2. Condition 1: (x + 6)(y - 4) = xy
   xy - 4x + 6y - 24 = xy
   -4x + 6y = 24 => -2x + 3y = 12.  (Equation 1)
3. Condition 2: (x - 10)(y + 10) = xy
   xy + 10x - 10y - 100 = xy
   10x - 10y = 100 => x - y = 10 => x = y + 10.  (Equation 2)
4. Substitute Equation 2 into Equation 1:
   -2(y + 10) + 3y = 12
   -2y - 20 + 3y = 12
   y = 32 days.
5. Find x:
   x = 32 + 10 = 42 men.
6. Check work: W = 42 × 32 = 1,344 man-days.
   (42 + 6)(32 - 4) = 48 × 28 = 1,344.
   (42 - 10)(32 + 10) = 32 × 42 = 1,344. Perfect!
7. Value of (x + y) = 42 + 32 = 74.$q$,
    $q$Eq 1: -2x + 3y = 12. Eq 2: x - y = 10. Multiply Eq 2 by 2: 2x - 2y = 20. Add to Eq 1: y = 32. Then x = 42. x + y = 74.$q$,
